## 7. BACKEND API CONTRACTS (MVP 2+)
FastAPI under /api/v1/. All list endpoints support ?patch= query param.
GET /api/v1/heroes                          -> HeroStats[]
GET /api/v1/heroes/{hero_id}                -> HeroStats (with map breakdown)
GET /api/v1/heroes/{hero_id}/history        -> { patch, win_rate, pick_rate }[]
GET /api/v1/meta?patch=&role=&rank=         -> { heroes, generated_at }
GET /api/v1/recommendations?role=&rank=&map=-> Recommendation[] top 3
GET /api/v1/patches                         -> Patch[] newest first
GET /api/v1/patches/{patch_id}              -> Patch with hero_changes
GET /api/v1/maps                            -> Map[]
GET /api/v1/maps/{map_id}/heroes            -> { hero_id, name, win_rate, pick_rate }[]

## 8. DATABASE TABLES (PostgreSQL — MVP 2+)
heroes: id TEXT PK, name, role (Vanguard|Duelist|Strategist), portrait_url, created_at
hero_stats: id SERIAL PK, hero_id FK, patch, rank_band, win_rate, pick_rate,
  ban_rate, avg_kda, sample_size, recorded_at. UNIQUE(hero_id, patch, rank_band)
hero_map_stats: id SERIAL PK, hero_id FK, map_id FK, patch, win_rate, pick_rate,
  sample_size, recorded_at. UNIQUE(hero_id, map_id, patch)
maps: id TEXT PK, name, game_mode (Domination|Convoy|Convergence), created_at
patches: id TEXT PK, label, released_at DATE, notes TEXT, is_major BOOL
patch_hero_changes: id SERIAL PK, patch_id FK, hero_id FK,
  change_type (buff|nerf|rework|new), description

## 9. DATA INGESTION FLOW (MVP 3+)
MarvelRivalsAPI.com -> APScheduler job every 6h
-> FastAPI worker: fetch batch, aggregate by hero+patch (NO player UIDs stored),
   upsert hero_stats + hero_map_stats, invalidate Redis keys
-> PostgreSQL primary store
-> Redis cache TTL 30min: meta:{patch}:{rank}, heroes:{id}, recs:{role}:{rank}:{map}

## 10. RECOMMENDATION SCORING MODEL (MVP 4+)
score = (win_rate * 0.45) + (pick_rate * 0.20)
      + (map_win_rate * 0.25) + (patch_delta * 0.10)
Only heroes matching selected role. Exclude sample_size < 500.
Return top 3 by score with template-generated reasoning text.

## 11. PRIVACY RULES (ALL STAGES)
1. No player-level data displayed.
2. No player UIDs stored anywhere.
3. No third-party tracking (no GA, no Meta Pixel).
4. Only documented MarvelRivalsAPI.com endpoints used.
5. Ingestion rate-limited with exponential back-off.

## 12. FEATURES OUT OF SCOPE
- Player profile / account lookup
- Live match tracking / real-time overlay
- User accounts, auth, saved preferences
- Monetisation, ads, premium tiers
- Community features (comments, ratings, forums)
- Mobile app
- Hero ability / lore content
- OAuth login

## 13. FUTURE ROADMAP
v2: URL-persisted rank params + shareable links, Discord/email patch alerts
v3: Patch comparison slider, synergy matrix heatmap
v4: Map-pool rotation tracker, tier list PNG export
v5: Streamer embed widget, public rate-limited JSON API

## 14. CODING CONVENTIONS
- Package manager: npm
- Framework: Next.js 15 App Router
- Language: TypeScript strict mode
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 (no CSS modules, no inline style props)
- Charts: Recharts
- Tables: TanStack Table v8
- Icons: lucide-react
- Class merging: clsx
- Dark-first: bg-gray-950 base, text-gray-100 primary text
- Brand accent: red-500 (#ef4444)
- Secondary accent: amber-400 (tier S / top performers)
- Chart palette: ['#ef4444','#f97316','#eab308','#22c55e','#3b82f6','#a855f7']
- Named exports only (no default exports from type files)
- NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix for client-safe env vars
- Backend: FastAPI on :8000, Next.js on :3000

